[ SECTOR_09 // SIGNAL_STUTTER ]

## [ 0x00_MISSION_BRIEF ]

Concept: String Parsing / Deduplication
Threat Level: EASY
Preamble: A damaged orbital relay is broadcasting redundant data packets. You must clean the raw signal by removing any consecutive duplicate characters before feeding it into your decrypter.

[ 0x01_LORE ]

While tapping into the Militech orbital comms relay, you notice the data stream is severely lagging. A physical malfunction in the relay's hardware is causing a transmission stutter, sending the exact same data byte multiple times in a row. If you feed this raw, bloated stream into your cyberdeck's decryption module, it will cause a buffer overflow and crash your system, alerting the sysadmins. You must write a lightweight filter algorithm to compress all consecutive identical characters into a single instance, restoring the original payload.

[ 0x02_OBJECTIVE ]

Read a string from standard input. Remove any consecutive duplicate characters from the string. Output the cleaned string. Note that the filter is case-sensitive (e.g., 'a' and 'A' are different characters).

[ 0x03_INPUT_STDIN ]

Line 1: A single string S containing letters, numbers, and symbols.

[ 0x04_OUTPUT_STDOUT ]

Print the cleaned string S with consecutive duplicates removed.

[ 0x05_CONSTRAINTS ]

1 <= length of S <= 100,000

S can contain uppercase and lowercase English letters, digits, and standard ASCII symbols.

Execution time limit: 1.0s

Memory limit: 64 MB

[ 0x06_EXAMPLES ]

Example 1

Input:
XXYYYZZZ-11122

Output:
XYZ-12

Example 2

Input:
SSyysstteemm_OOnnlliinnee

Output:
System_Online
